{
  "raw_notes": "Patient Name: Jane Doe\nDOB: 01/15/1975\n\n**Subjective:**\nPatient presents with general malaise and fatigue for the past 3 days. She reports a cough, which she describes as 'dry and irritating'. She thinks she might have had a fever yesterday, 'around 100 degrees, but not sure if it was exactly 100'. Reports she's been taking Tylenol, 500 mg every 6 hours, for the malaise. She states she has an allergy to 'penicillin or maybe amoxicillin, not sure which one, but it caused a rash last time'. No other medical history reported. Denies shortness of breath. No known drug allergies besides the uncertain penicillin/amoxicillin. Last menstrual period 2 weeks ago.\n\n**Objective:**\nGeneral: Appears tired but in no acute distress.\nLungs: Clear to auscultation bilaterally. No wheezes or crackles.\nThroat: Mild erythema, no exudates.\n\n**Assessment:**\nAcute bronchitis, likely viral.\n\n**Plan:**\n1. Continue supportive care. \n2. Consider chest X-ray if cough worsens.\n3. Patient to follow up in 5 days or sooner if symptoms change.",
